==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|en|authentic|ity}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US|caught-cot}} {{IPA|en|/ɑθɛnˈtɪsɪti/|/ɑθənˈtɪsɪti/|[ɑθɛnˈtɪsɪɾi]|[ɑθənˈtɪsɪɾi]}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|+}}

# The quality of being [[genuine]] or not corrupted from the original, of having the same origin (or attribution, commitment, intention, etc.) as claimed.
#: {{ux|en|I hereby certify the '''authenticity''' of this copy.}}
#: {{ux|en|The '''authenticity''' of this painting is questionable.}}
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|year=2018|author=James Lambert|title=A multitude of ‘lishes’: The nomenclature of hybridity|journal=English World-Wide|page=2
|url=https://www.researchgate.net/publication/318367113_A_multitude_of_lishes_The_nomenclature_of_hybridity
|text=Urban Dictionary records at least 66 of the terms found by the present research, but as this dictionary liberally accepts words, definitions, and sample sentences based solely on the say-so of contributors, in the absence of corroboration from other sources the '''authenticity''' of some entries must remain dubious.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} The quality of being [[authentic]] (of established [[authority]]).

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|quality of being genuine}} {{l|en|genuineness}}

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|quality of not being genuine}} {{l|en|phoniness}}; [[forgery]]; [[fakeness]]; [[bogosity]]

